/* =====================================================================================================
 * Forest — VERSION STAMPS (single source of truth).
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * TWO stamps, tracking two independent things (operator directive S12.11xx). Keeping them separate lets
 * Shea see at a glance WHICH element of the viewer changed:
 *
 *   • FOREST_SHELL_VERSION — the VIEWER-WINDOW / skin version. Shown small in the top bar (right side,
 *     just left of the lock). Increments when we introduce a set of changes to the whole LOOK & FEEL —
 *     a skin/theme change to the viewer window. It does NOT move when only an app's internals change.
 *
 *   • FOREST_APP_VERSION — the per-app (email/calendar/contacts) stamp. Shown small under the "Mail"
 *     title in the mail pane (mail-renderer.js) and its siblings. Increments only when the ACTUAL APP
 *     changes — not on a skin change.
 *
 * Origin of the per-app stamp: operator directive — a visible number confirms the current code
 * is the one that's live.
 *
 * DEPLOY SEAM — RECONCILED. This note used to say the bump-guard "must be taught to accept
 * either published stamp bumped." It already has been: version-bump-guard.sh --mode publish passes when
 * EITHER declared stamp is strictly newer than the box, and refuses only when NEITHER moved (the
 * forgotten-bump case) or when a declared stamp would go BACKWARDS (a stale-commit downgrade). So a
 * skin-only deploy bumps FOREST_SHELL_VERSION alone and passes. The stale note is repaired rather than
 * left, because a comment that tells the next deploy-er a live guard is broken when it is not costs a
 * session: 's Compose fix landed on main and sat UNSERVED because neither stamp moved, and this
 * note was the reason nobody bumped the one that would have shipped it.
 * ===================================================================================================== */
