/* ═══ THE PER-APP MAP IS GONE (— the fold) ═══════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * There WAS a `window.FOREST_APP_VERSIONS` map here: a hand-kept mirror of each renderer module's
 * own `_version`, so each app could show its OWN number in the left column (operator directive
 *). It is deleted. Not corrected — DELETED.
 *
 * WHY. It drifted three times in three sessions. This file's own comment warned that it would
 * ("⚠ THIS MAP IS A HAND-KEPT MIRROR. It DRIFTS."), and it drifted anyway — and then SHIPPED
 * wrong (the box served contacts-renderer 1.12.0 while the map told Shea "1.10.0"). The third
 * strike was a PARALLEL collision: two live sessions independently stamped calendar-renderer
 * 1.6.0 for different work and both claimed aggregate 1.28. A version stamp exists for exactly
 * one purpose — to let the operator confirm the code he is looking at is the code that is live.
 * A stamp that is WRONG is worse than no stamp: it is a confident false answer to the one
 * question the stamp exists to answer.
 *
 * A comment is not a guard (Graham). A red parity test was a floor-raise, not a seal — it made
 * the drift LOUD while the mirror survived, and a guard that reports and does not block is a
 * decoration with good intentions.
 *
 * THE FIX IS SUBTRACTION. `shell/pane.js appVersion(kind)` now reads the number straight off the
 * live renderer module — `window.ForestShell[kind + "Renderer"]._version` — resolved by the SAME
 * naming convention `shell-renderers.js registerAll` already uses to find those modules. The
 * number the pane shows IS the number in the renderer file. There is no second copy, so the two
 * copies cannot disagree. The drift is not defended against; it is not expressible.
 *
 * WHAT THIS MEANS WHEN YOU BUILD. Touch a renderer's `_version`. That is the whole ritual. You do
 * not touch this file. The convention is pinned by `shell/version-stamp-derived.test.js` — a new
 * app kind whose module is not named `<kind>Renderer`, or which carries no `_version`, goes red.
 *
 * WHAT DID NOT CHANGE. The two stamps ABOVE are untouched and still hand-kept on purpose:
 *   • FOREST_APP_VERSION  — the AGGREGATE, read by forest/deploy/version-bump-guard.sh. It GATES
 *     the deploy, so it must be a bare M.N a shell script can compare. Bump it every deploy.
 *   • FOREST_SHELL_VERSION — the viewer-window skin version.
 * The aggregate is a hand-kept scalar with no allocator, so two parallel sessions can still
 * collide on it — that is a DIFFERENT fault, and the bump-guard is what catches it today. This
 * fold closes the MAP's drift, not the scalar's.
 * Owed: forest-per-app-version-map-hand-kept-drift — CLOSED here.
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
